Every class can eventually get acceptable fail rates with ID when stripped of 
metal armor.  The benefit to the special spell is reduced fail rates.  
Rangers would be able to cast ID reliably sooner than other combat classes 
(but probably not sooner than W, P, M), and not have to take off so much 
armor.  That's all.

Note that the ranger still has to:
-find a spellbook of ID
-read it successfully
-spend 15 mana per casting

...just like the other classes do.


